{"In handleCancelBooking.ts, deleteScheduledEmailReminder is invoked without await and without handling its result, risking unhandled rejections": 0.5838770866394043, "When immediateDelete is true, deleteScheduledEmailReminder cancels via SendGrid but returns without deleting or updating the workflowReminder row in Prisma, leaving orphaned records that can grow unboundedly": 0.9604554176330566, "Email cancellation relies on a cancelled flag and cron-based finalization, while SMS cancellation immediately deletes the DB row via Twilio with no flag-based fallback, producing divergent behavior and potential timing issues": 0.7492809891700745, "No visible test coverage for the cron job that cancels cancelled reminders, and edge cases such as reminders cancelled with immediateDelete flag or reminders cancelled but with null referenceId are not tested": 0.1971580982208252, "Several code paths use immediateDelete=true without setting the cancelled flag, meaning those reminders are never picked up by the cron job scheduleEmailReminders that relies on cancelled: true to finalize cancellations": 0.8435726761817932, "WorkflowReminder.cancelled field is defined as Boolean? with no default, so existing and newly inserted rows can hold NULL, which cron logic filtering on cancelled: true silently treats as not-cancelled": 0.7553036212921143}